speechtext:
I would
ask my hon. friend to leave it in the estimates. I anticipate that I can make a number of savings on these salaries. Perhaps we shall have to pay them for one, two or three months-I do not know how long- but you must provide for the salaries until the resignations take effect, and I have to ask the committee to vote them. It is asking a minister to d'o the impossible to clear out these employees on the 31st March and make these savings. Many of these men are waiting, of course, for the passing of the Superannuation Act. My hon. friend may say:	You should not allow them to wait;
but as I pointed out, these are old and trusted employees who have rendered good service and I think they are entitled to some consideration.
